# Cursor Rules for Jekyll Blog Project

## Project Overview
This is a Jekyll-based blog website using the Hydeout theme. The project contains travel blog posts about different countries and regions around the world.

## File Structure
- `_posts/`: Contains all blog posts in Markdown format with YAML front matter
- `_layouts/`: Jekyll layout templates
- `_includes/`: Reusable HTML components
- `_sass/`: SCSS stylesheets for the Hydeout theme
- `assets/`: Static assets including images (PNG, JPEG, JPG)
- `_site/`: Generated static site (should not be edited directly)

## Coding Standards

### Markdown Posts
- Use YAML front matter for metadata
- Include proper tags and categories
- Use descriptive filenames with date prefix (YYYY-MM-DD-Title.md)
- Include relevant images in assets folder
- Use proper heading hierarchy (H1, H2, H3)

### HTML/Liquid Templates
- Follow Jekyll Liquid syntax conventions
- Use semantic HTML5 elements
- Maintain consistent indentation (2 spaces)
- Include proper meta tags and SEO elements

### SCSS/CSS
- Follow BEM methodology for class naming
- Use SCSS features like variables, mixins, and nesting
- Maintain responsive design principles
- Follow the existing Hydeout theme structure

### JavaScript
- Use vanilla JavaScript or minimal dependencies
- Follow modern ES6+ syntax when possible
- Ensure accessibility and performance

## AI Assistant Guidelines

### When Creating New Posts
- Suggest appropriate tags and categories based on content
- Include proper YAML front matter structure
- Recommend relevant images from assets folder
- Follow the existing post naming convention

### When Modifying Templates
- Maintain the Hydeout theme's design principles
- Preserve existing functionality
- Test changes across different page types
- Consider mobile responsiveness

### When Working with Assets
- Optimize images for web use
- Use descriptive filenames
- Maintain consistent image dimensions when possible
- Consider lazy loading for performance

### Code Quality
- Write clean, readable code
- Add comments for complex logic
- Follow existing code style and patterns
- Test changes locally before suggesting

## Common Tasks
- Creating new blog posts about countries/regions
- Adding new images to assets folder
- Modifying theme styling
- Updating site configuration
- Optimizing performance and SEO

## Dependencies
- Jekyll 4.3.3
- Hydeout theme
- Stylelint for SCSS linting
- Ruby gems specified in Gemfile

## Build Process
- Use `bundle exec jekyll serve` for local development
- Use `bundle exec jekyll build` for production build
- Run `npm run stylelint` to check SCSS code quality

## Notes
- The _site directory is generated and should not be manually edited
- Images are stored in assets/ and referenced in posts
- The project uses GitHub Pages for hosting
- Maintain consistent formatting across all content files
